          <text id="/data/results_group/res_impetigo:label">
            <value>Impetigo or Folliculitis</value>
          </text>
          <text id="/data/results_group/res_impetigo_action:label">
            <value>The child may have Impetigo or Folliculitis.\n\nProcedure:\n- Clean sores with antiseptic\n- Drain pus if fluctuant\n- Start cloxacillin sirup (125mg/5ml) if size &gt;4cm or red streaks or tender nodes or multiple abscesses for 5 days (50mg/kg every 6 hours)\n- Refer URGENTLY if child has fever and / or if infection extends to the muscle\n- Apply antibiotic cream – triple antibiotic ointment</value>
          </text>
          <text id="/data/results_group/res_ring_worm:label">
            <value>Ring Worm (Tinea)</value>
          </text>
          <text id="/data/results_group/res_ring_worm_action:label">
            <value>The child may have Ring Worm.\n\nProcedure:\n- If limited to a few patches: Grisefulvine or Ketoconazole cream\n- If extensive give: Ketoconazole 2-12month(6-10kg): 40mg/day 12mo-5yrs: 60 mg/day Or if: Age &gt;2: give griseofulvin, tablets, 125 mg with fatty meal (10mg/kg/day), 2 tablets once a day for 6 weeks\n- If in hair: shave hair, treat as above\n- If infected (red, warm, pus) add cloxacilline</value>
          </text>
          <text id="/data/results_group/res_scabies:label">
            <value>Scabies</value>
          </text>
          <text id="/data/results_group/res_scabies_action:label">
            <value>The child may have Scabies.\n\nProcedure:\n- Treat itching: Calamine lotion\n- Apply: 25% topical Benzyl Benzoate at night, repeat for 3 days after washing.\n- Council hygiene measures: treat all people in the household who are affected, wash bed linen and clothes with warm water and put in the sun, wash affected persons\n- When infected add cloxaciline</value>
          </text>
          <text id="/data/results_group/res_severe_malnutrition_anemia:label">
            <value>Moderate or Severe Acute Malnutrition with Anemia</value>
          </text>
          <text id="/data/results_group/res_severe_malnutrition_anemia_action:label">
            <value>The child may have moderate or severe acute malnutrition with anemia.\n\nProcedure:\n- Refer to malnutrition clinic\n- Iron-Folic Acid tablets – 1 per day</value>
          </text>
          <text id="/data/results_group/res_severe_anemia:label">
            <value>Severe Anemia</value>
          </text>
          <text id="/data/results_group/res_severe_anemia_action:label">
            <value>The child may have severe anemia.\n\nProcedure:\n- Iron folic acid\n- Refer for investigation</value>
          </text>
          <text id="/data/results_group/res_moderate_anemia:label">
            <value>Moderate Anemia</value>
          </text>
          <text id="/data/results_group/res_moderate_anemia_action:label">
            <value>The child may have moderate anemia.\n\nProcedure:\n- Iron, folic acid – 1 tablet once a day, give for 14 days\n- Albendazole (400 mg) 12-23 months – ½ co every 6 months 24-59 months – 1 co every 6 months\n- Nutrition counseling: green leaves, fruits, rasped carots and red beet</value>
          </text>
